(3) there is a rearrangement $\left(b_{1}, b_{2}, \ldots, b_{2020}\right)$ of $\left(a_{1}, a_{2}, \ldots, a_{2020}\right)$ such that
$$
\sum_{i=1}^{2020}\left(\left(a_{i}+1\right)\left(b_{i}+1\right)\right)^{2} = 4 \sum_{i=1}^{2020} a_{i}^{3}
$$
A rearrangement means the same numbers in a different order. For instance, $\left(2,1,2\right)$ is a rearrangement of $\left(1,2,2\right)$, and they are both rearrangements of $\left(2,2,1\right)$. Note that any sequence is a rearrangement of itself.

